    "title": "2026 RBC Heritage TV schedule, coverage: Where to watch, live stream first signature event after Masters",
    "text": "Getty Images After Rory McIlroy's historic win at the 2026 Masters, the PGA Tour schedule rolls along with the fourth signature event of the season at the RBC Heritage. Many of the world's best have made the short trip over from Augusta, Georgia, to Hilton Head Island, South Carolina, to take their shot at a restored Harbour Town Golf Links.While McIlroy is taking the week off after capturing back-to-back green jackets, most of the PGA Tour's top players are in action. That includes Scottie Scheffler and Cameron Young, fresh off top-five finishes at the Masters, who are looking to carry some positive momentum into Harbour Town. Follow 2026 RBC Heritage leaderboard coverage with live updates in Round 4.Matt Fitzpatrick and Scottie Scheffler are fighting it out to the finish, each looking for his second win of the season, though it has been Fitzpatrick standing atop to this point at RBC Heritage as holder of the 36- and 54-hole leads.Here's how you can watch play all week at Pete Dye's gem on the South Carolina shore. 2026 RBC Heritage TV scheduleAll times Eastern Round 4 - SundayRound 4 starts: 7 a.m. [Tee times]PGA Tour Live: 7 a.m. - 6 p.m. -- PGA Tour LiveEarly TV coverage: 1-3 p.m. on Golf ChannelEarly streaming: 1-3 p.m. on GolfChannel.comLive TV coverage: 3-6 p.m. on CBS, Paramount+Live streaming: 3-6 p.m. on CBSSports.com, CBS Sports App Radio: 1-6 p.m. -- PGA Tour Radio",
